# Packages installed on request that are deliberately declared in no Brewfile.
#
# `assay`'s `brew-health` station reads this file, so a decision recorded here stops
# resurfacing — the same role `yadm/unmanaged` plays for tracking coverage. A
# name listed here is one that must NOT be reproduced on the next machine; a
# package that should be is declared in a Brewfile instead, and a package that is
# neither is uninstalled.
#
# One entry per line, `<name>  # reason`. `#` comments and blank lines ignored.
# Formulae and casks share the namespace, as they do in a Brewfile.
